[5] No talk talk, let's talk talk! Once upon a time, there was a tiny little bakery tucked away in a quiet corner of a bustling city. The sign above the door read "Sweet Delights" and the smell of fresh baked goods wafted out onto the sidewalk, enticing passersby to come and investigate.

I stumbled upon this little gem one morning, just as the sun was rising over the skyscrapers. The owner, a warm and welcoming woman named Sophie, was already hard at work preparing for the day's customers. She had a way of making everyone feel like they were the only person in the world, even though she was bustling around like a madwoman getting everything just so.

As I pushed open the door, Sophie looked up and smiled brightly, her eyes twinkling with warmth. "Good morning! Welcome to Sweet Delights! What brings you to our humble bakery today?" she asked, her voice like butter melting on toast.

