[4] No sooner had the thought crossed my mind than a figure appeared out of the shadows, watching me with piercing green eyes. I felt a shiver run down my spine as we stood there, frozen in time, waiting to see what would happen next.

Just as suddenly as he had appeared, the figure vanished into thin air, leaving me feeling both relieved and confused. I couldn't shake the feeling that I had just had a glimpse into a world beyond our own, a world where magic was real and anything could happen.

I looked around nervously, wondering if anyone had seen what had just happened, but I was alone. Just me, standing there feeling like a fool for thinking that maybe, just maybe, something supernatural had tried to make contact with me.

I took a deep breath and tried to shake off the feeling, telling myself it was just my imagination playing tricks on me. But deep down, I knew something weird had just happened, and I couldn't wait to find out what it was
